      "key": {
        "uuid": "6b46b03e_91f72699",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NattSocketKeepalive.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-07T18:28:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we actually need a start method? RAII seems like a much tidier pattern, and it makes things like try-with-resources work as intended. Then people can do things like:\n\ntry (NattSocketKeepalive \u003d new NattSocketKeepalive(...)) {\n    // go to sleep here.\n    while(!recv(longTimeout)) {\n        doDpd();\n    }\n} except (DpdException dpdE) {\n    log(\"something went wrong\");\n}",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "7d1123c5994f3a93c3172a1ffdc8b834d10bfa8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7b6b3c10_861d38d7",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NattSocketKeepalive.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-08T08:05:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agree it is tidier pattern, but does it make people be less aware they are using ConnectivityService?\nAnd since we are still want people to do things inside callback,\nuse start also let people don\u0027t have to put every necessary params and callbacks everytime.\nBut I don\u0027t have strong opinion about this.\n+lorenzo@, any thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "6b46b03e_91f72699",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "7d1123c5994f3a93c3172a1ffdc8b834d10bfa8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e0f4c358_fd747366",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NattSocketKeepalive.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-17T09:30:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "An explicit start() method also allows calling start() after stop(). This might not be super useful for NAT-T, but it would make sense for TCP. If we support start() after stop() for TCP, then we probably want to have an explicit start() method here for consistency.",
      "parentUuid": "7b6b3c10_861d38d7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "7d1123c5994f3a93c3172a1ffdc8b834d10bfa8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2768cc7a_078166ea",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NattSocketKeepalive.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-17T19:33:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "*sigh* burdening NATT with a thus-far-unimplementable TCP keepalive\u0027s requirements. I\u0027ll say it again... this would all be a much smaller cleaner surface if we did it in IpSecManager, even if IpSecManager used 20 lines of callback skeleton for the user to override (though I think the callback itself can/should be simplified... you can take a look at the onError callback scheme that to see what I just did for CellInfo based on 2 of the other API councilors\u0027 suggestions).\n\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/master/telephony/java/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.java#4872\n\nI\u0027ve made throwables Parcelable so that we don\u0027t have to commit to all the error codes up front, since it doesn\u0027t matter to the caller for anything other than debug, unless the error code is actionable.",
      "parentUuid": "e0f4c358_fd747366",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "7d1123c5994f3a93c3172a1ffdc8b834d10bfa8e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
