      "writtenOn": "2019-01-07T18:28:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the looper isn\u0027t directly used by this class, it\u0027s odd to have the error condition here stop the looper. Is there a way to refactor so that this class doesn\u0027t deal with the looper?\n\nSide note: the entire thread isn\u0027t needed anyway. You can either remove it entirely and use the binder thread or (less good) use the ConnectivityManager thread.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7d1123c5994f3a93c3172a1ffdc8b834d10bfa8e",
