    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d6a1b85c_d3f90616",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NattSocketKeepalive.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-21T03:54:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In my mind this is mostly a matter of documentation. If this API requires the executor to have some specific properties (e.g. non-inline) then either :\n・Failure to comply with these requirements only affects the client-visible. Then the requirements should simply be documented ; if the client passes a bad executor it\u0027s on them.\n・Failure to comply has more severe ramifications (e.g. crashing the system). Then the implementation needs to either provide these guarantees (e.g. by wrapping the executor) or to check the executor actually provides them (keep in mind most executors can be reconfigured at runtime).",
      "parentUuid": "fff11763_cd7b5cf9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7d1123c5994f3a93c3172a1ffdc8b834d10bfa8e",
